<%# Layout for the unattended wall display. No navbar, sidebar, modal frame, or
    toasts -- no one is standing at this screen to use them, and every pixel
    belongs to the board.

    Dark is fixed here rather than followed from the viewer's setting: the
    monitor this runs on has no one to flip a switch, and a white screen in a
    dim room is unreadable. Both the class and the attribute are set, because
    the two halves of the theme system read different ones -- the `dark:`
    variants key off the class, and the colour tokens key off data-theme. %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="dark" data-theme="dark">
<head>
  <title><%= content_for(:title) || "Ranger Secret Clubhouse" %></title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
  <%# Arrive here the long way round -- a fresh load, not a swap of the page
      body. The dark theme and the missing chrome are both set on the <html>
      element, which is the one part of the page a Turbo visit leaves alone, so
      following the menu link here would otherwise leave the monitor showing
      the board in whatever theme the last page was using. %>
  <meta name="turbo-visit-control" content="reload">
  <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
  <%= csp_meta_tag %>
  <%# The proportional roman latin face is on the critical path for every page. The
      italic, latin-ext and monospaced faces are declared in fonts.css and fetched
      only when something actually asks for them. %>
  <link rel="preload" href="<%= asset_path("atkinson-latin.woff2") %>" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <%= stylesheet_link_tag "tailwind", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
  <%= javascript_importmap_tags %>
  <%# Stimulus's own entry modules. They are inside the lazily-pinned controllers
      directory, so without these two the browser only discovers them after
      application.js has been fetched and parsed. %>
  <link rel="modulepreload" href="<%= asset_path("controllers/index.js") %>">
  <link rel="modulepreload" href="<%= asset_path("controllers/application.js") %>">
</head>
<body class="bg-base-100 text-base-content" data-controller="local-time">
<%= yield %>
</body>
</html>
